A||N||2||Seanh||Should I paint my car myself?||||1||
Z||000000||Seanh||09-15-2001||04:31 PM||||I am going to repaint my either this winter, or next spring, and plan on atleast doing all the prep work myself, if not all of it. I have a fairly descent compressed air paint sprayer, but no idea on how to use it properly. Are there any good sites on painting the car yourself out there? Please post anything you think might be useful.<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 4spd Auto, getting ready to install T-6 turbo.||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||09-15-2001||05:30 PM||||its not that hard, just practice. Paint lawnmowers, wagons, anything. Its more of a hands on thing, you cant learn to do it by reading manuals. I started when I used spray cans to paint model cars. Now I moved up, Ive even painted LearJets now.||||reg||1
Z||000002||gunshelb1||09-15-2001||06:27 PM||||Of course you should do it yourself...<BR>A paint gun only costs about $100 and the filter plus mask is about $40, and paint can vary widely.  But you'll get a better job if you paint it yourself, just talk to your local paint supplier and they will give you detailed instructions.  Of course it all takes a lot of time to do the prep and the paint.  Plan on spending a good 8 hours painting and clearcoating.  But overall its worth it. ||||reg||1
